/E (This study explores the differences in attitudinal loyalty toward full-service carriers and low-cost carriers among Generation X, Y, and Z in Taiwan. The research analyzes how safety perception, service expectations, travel motivation, and digital interaction influence airline preferences across generations. Findings suggest that Gen X demonstrates stronger loyalty toward full-service airlines, while Gen Z shows greater psychological attachment to low-cost carriers due to digital convenience and perceived cost-performance value.)
