/E (We examined three core issues. The first one is about Taiwan, as Taiwan has a smaller population and market size, which may limit its overall sales. Secondly, Taiwan has an active marathon community. Brands like HOKA, Adidas and Oncloud have gained significant market traction in Taiwan's running community, building a strong reputation for comfort and design, creating a strong competitor for Nike in the running shoe market, directly attacking Nike's core performance segment. Lastly, Nike's premium pricing, which may be highly effective in the U.S, but in Taiwan where there are plenty of students and middle class consumers. It may seem quite expensive, where Taiwanese people often emphasis on International brands and value for money items, compared with the American consumers who are generally more accepting of premium pricing.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [2]
>>
