/E (In conclusion, even a single month of consecutive hourly data can reveal useful temporal structures in multiple air pollutants. Higher-order polynomial models offer greater flexibility than a simple quadratic for all pollutants examined. A full year of data would be required to examine seasonal cycles or rare pollution episodes. This study demonstrates that comparative polynomial modeling of government air quality data can effectively identify high-pollution periods and provide insights to support targeted air quality management in Taichung City.)
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [3]
>>
